course: dictionary
lesson: 4295
title: A grid of squares
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A grid is a pattern of straight lines that cross each other and make squares. «A digital picture is a grid of tiny coloured squares called pixels.» Each square in that grid is one tiny dot of colour in the picture.
explain: In maths, grids help you count, find places and multiply. «Counting on a drawing grid» means counting the squares to find how big a shape is. The grid method splits a big multiplication into smaller boxes that are easier to add up.
explain: The word grid can mean other things too. «All the power stations and homes are joined in one big web called the grid» means the network of wires that carries electricity. A metal grid over a drain is a frame of bars. Read the words around grid to find which meaning fits.
fact: A grid is a pattern of straight lines crossing each other to make squares.
fact: On a map, a grid reference uses letters and numbers to show exactly where a place is.
fact: The grid method is a way to multiply big numbers by splitting them into smaller boxes.
fact: «The grid» can mean the network of wires that brings electricity to homes.
fact: A metal grid over a drain is a frame of bars that lets water through but stops large things falling in.
exercise: In «A digital picture is a grid of tiny coloured squares called pixels», what does grid mean? | *A pattern of straight lines crossing to make squares | A small bird that sings | A loud sound from a speaker | A kind of cloud
exercise: On a map, a grid lets you find a place using what? | Colours and songs | Only words | Weight and time | *Letters and numbers
exercise: In maths, the grid method helps you do what? | Paint pictures | *Multiply bigger numbers | Tell the time | Spell long words
test: «All the power stations and homes are joined in one big web called the grid.» In this sentence, the grid means what? | A metal frame over a drain | A pattern of squares on paper | A pet's cage | *The network of wires that brings electricity to homes
test: A grid with 3 rows and 4 columns of squares has how many squares in total? | 7 | 34 | 3 | *12
exam: Which best describes a grid? | A single dot | *Straight lines crossing each other to make squares | A round ball | A single curved line
